The openSUSE Leap and SUSE Linux Enterprise Server configs now use a single template per major version (`opensuse-leap-15.tpl`, `opensuse-leap-16.tpl`, `sles-15.tpl` and `sles-16.tpl`), and each config file only sets the release and the architecture, like the Fedora ones. For the users of the configs:

- The EOL openSUSE Leap 15.0 to 15.4 configs now use `cdn.opensuse.org`, like the other openSUSE configs. This also fixes the updates repository of the openSUSE Leap 15.0 aarch64 config.
- The openSUSE Leap 15.0 to 15.2 bootstrap chroots are now installed from the Leap repositories, because there are no `leap-dnf` images for them. Before, they used the Fedora image, and mixed Fedora and Leap packages.
- All the openSUSE Leap 15 configs now trust the same GPG keys, the old and the new openSUSE and SUSE keys used across the 15.x releases.

See [PR#1849][] for the details.
